Package: yourhonor
Title: Calibrate Large Language Model Judges
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jay", "Clark", , "27960665+JsizzleR@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Treat a large language model used as an evaluator (an
    "LLM-as-judge") as a measurement instrument and report its
    psychometric properties. Given a judge and a set of human-labeled
    examples, 'yourhonor' reports chance-corrected agreement between the
    judge and humans (Cohen's kappa, Krippendorff's alpha and Gwet's
    AC1 and weighted AC2) with bootstrap confidence intervals,
    human-human reliability when several raters are supplied, per-class
    error intervals, structured paired bias probes and test-retest
    stability. Explicit
    acceptance policies turn evidence into conservative decisions, and
    versioned artifacts support portable aggregate audit review. It
    complements the 'ellmer' and 'vitals' evaluation stack: it does not
    run evaluations, it measures the judge that scores them.
